---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About NO BALL GAMES | From Restricted Spaces to Street Culture Brand"
  description="Learn the story behind NO BALL GAMES, a raw street-culture brand turning public restriction, graffiti energy and estate identity into a creative movement."
  current="about"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">About the brand</span>
    <h1>From a warning sign to a creative weapon.</h1>
    <p>
      NO BALL GAMES starts with a simple British street image: a sign telling people what they cannot do. The brand flips that message. It takes the restriction, the estate memory, the wall texture and the attitude, then turns it into identity.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section split-grid">
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">The meaning</span>
      <h2>Denied space becomes owned space.</h2>
      <p>
        The sign is supposed to shut down play. In this brand, it becomes the opposite: a reminder to create even when the space was never designed for you.
      </p>
      <p>
        NO BALL GAMES stands for people who grew up around hard concrete, rules, warnings, locked courts, blank walls and public spaces that felt controlled by everyone except the people living there.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">The energy</span>
      <ul class="list-clean">
        <li>Graffiti attitude without fake polish.</li>
        <li>British estate culture and urban memory.</li>
        <li>Grime art, streetwear, characters and collectibles.</li>
        <li>Digital-first culture without losing the real-world edge.</li>
        <li>A brand system that can expand into art, games, clothing and lore.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Brand rules</h2>
      <p>The site should feel clean enough to trust and raw enough to believe.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Rule one</span>
        <h3>No fake corporate voice</h3>
        <p>Keep the language direct, visual and culturally grounded. The brand should sound like it came from the wall, not a boardroom.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Rule two</span>
        <h3>Real culture first</h3>
        <p>Art, people, places, stories and community matter more than empty hype. Digital tools should support the culture, not replace it.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Rule three</span>
        <h3>Build with depth</h3>
        <p>Every page should add something: story, proof, context, product value, community value or collector value.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
